<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aqtaghliq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th–18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as White Mountain khojas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aqtaghliq, or 'White Mountain' faction, was one of two rival branches of the Naqshbandi khojas who dominated the religious and political life of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgaria">Kashgaria</a> in the 17th and 18th centuries. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afaq-khoja">Afaq Khoja</a> and his descendants, they contended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarataghliq">Qarataghliq</a> ('Black Mountain') khojas, and in 1680 invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> to conquer the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yarkent-khanate">Yarkent Khanate</a>. Their power ended with the Qing conquest of 1759.</p></div>
